# Deny everything, then allow only what the workspace build needs.
# docker/Dockerfile does `COPY . .` for the cargo-chef planner and builder,
# so this allowlist is the sole bound on context size.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo/

# Prebuilt release binaries staged at the repo root by .github/workflows/docker.yaml
# before invoking docker/Dockerfile.ci with `context: .`.
!bins/

!krikos/
!krikos-base/
!krikos-dns/
!krikos-dns-server/
!krikos-relay/
!krikos-resolver/
!krikos-runtime/
!tools/
!framework/
!examples/
!integration-tests/
!protocols/

# docker/Dockerfile COPYs the two [patch.crates-io] crates into rust_builder
# ahead of `cargo chef cook` (cargo reads their manifests directly off disk
# during dependency resolution; see the comment there). Those COPY sources
# are nested (vendor/<crate>), but check-docker-context.sh's COPY-derived
# requirement only inspects the top-level path segment, so a bare `!vendor/`
# is required here in addition to the two specific entries below. Re-exclude
# the rest of vendor/ so that doesn't widen the context beyond what's
# needed: vendor/rustls-0.23.41 is patched in by krikos-sim and fuzz only,
# neither of which this image builds, and the *.patch files/README are
# provenance docs, not build inputs.
!vendor/
vendor/rustls-0.23.41/
vendor/*.patch
vendor/README.md
!vendor/hickory-server-0.26.1/
!vendor/noq-1.1.0/

# Re-exclude build output inside the directories allowed above.
**/target
